The new nonce prefixes and a new output-witness field require a hard fork because old parsers reject them.
A soft fork cannot make those rejected encodings valid.
The existing-field alternatives avoid that parsing change, but need rules for locating each ciphertext and preventing its removal or replacement.
The nonce extension uses more block space than witness placements in exchange for carrying the ciphertext directly in the output that signatures already commit to.

<span id="cost-of-the-hke-nonce"></span>
